==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 4~20 seconds<sup>120f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**3 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 1~4 seconds<sup>30f~120f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**3 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 1~4 seconds<sup>30f~120f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**3 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 1~4 seconds<sup>30f~120f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This becomes an easy fight with some decent meatshielding and stacking [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attack]] like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]. Owlbrow's range is only 340 and he attacks fairly slowly, so he gets outranged by plenty of cats and is relatively easy to stall and kill. [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]], [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] are all non-[[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha]] cats that can stay out of reach if the Owlbrows are properly stalled.

Strictly speaking, the occasionally spawning Gory Dark is probably more dangerous to an unprepared player than all of the Owlbrows that show up, but the ranged attackers you use to defeat the Owlbrows will likely already double as Gory Dark counters, so there's no need to bring [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark units]].

Bring two or three meatshields and the mentioned cats above and you're golden.

